# NOITE's hall (3fhall) starts the real TIRO, which loses: 0x40a lost with
# -1050 (a negative score lowers NOITE's), a life less, back to the hall.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fhall --ms 30000 --input tools/play/tiro-3fhall-lose.input
#
# As tiro-3fhall-win: WinExec at 2000, TIRO starts at 3500; the shots are
# `tools/tiro_plan.py --start 3500 --lose`. Same game with `--fix all`.
2000 rclick 80 200
3000 expect 3fhall
# shot 1: straight, traveco
3680 key right
3800 key space
4000 dump tiro
# shot 2: straight, traveco
5070 key space
# shot 3: straight, hits nothing
6340 key space
# shot 4: straight, traveco
8330 key space
# shot 5: right, hits nothing
9480 key right
9600 key space
# shot 6: straight, traveco
10530 key left
10650 key space
# shot 7: straight, hits nothing
11870 key space
# shot 8: straight, hits nothing
13360 key space
# shot 9: straight, hits nothing
15350 key space
# shot 10: straight, traveco
17340 key space
# shot 11: straight, traveco
18560 key space
# shot 12: straight, hits nothing
19560 key space
# shot 13: right, hits nothing
21430 key right
21550 key space
# shot 14: right, traveco
23590 key space
# shot 15: straight, TIRO ends at the next target tick
24800 key left
24920 key space
25100 result lost -1050
25100 expect 3fhall
26000 state
26000 dump hall
